-- smucclaw/l4-ide#1081, found by an independent re-check: a lapse of a deadline
-- FIXED at the outset, inside an EVERY (fork). The tenants' deadline is 6 from
-- the outset; the landlord's refund is 2 after a miss (8). Pia's act starts
-- Rex's deadline 3 after it, so Pia signing at 5 puts Rex's deadline on the
-- refund at 8.
IMPORT prelude
DECLARE Actor IS ONE OF
    Landlord HAS name IS A STRING
    Tenant   HAS name IS A STRING
DECLARE Action IS ONE OF
    Sign    HAS signer IS AN Actor
    Refund  HAS who    IS AN Actor

lord  MEANS Landlord OF "Lord"
rex   MEANS Landlord OF "Rex"
pia   MEANS Landlord OF "Pia"
bob   MEANS Tenant OF "Bob"
carol MEANS Tenant OF "Carol"

GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
fxfork MEANS
       (EVERY Tenant t IN LIST bob, carol
          MUST   Sign t
          WITHIN 6
          UPON   EACH
          HENCE  FULFILLED
          LEST   (PARTY lord MUST Refund lord WITHIN 2 HENCE FULFILLED LEST BREACH BY lord))
  RAND (PARTY pia MUST Sign pia WITHIN 9
          HENCE (PARTY rex MUST Sign rex WITHIN 3 HENCE FULFILLED LEST BREACH BY rex)
          LEST BREACH BY pia)

#TRACE fxfork AT 0 WITH
  PARTY pia DOES Sign pia AT 5
  (WAITUNTIL 7)
